    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="0755" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg749"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Coleman.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 545.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information copies of
                    recent correspondence between the Department and the British and German
                    legations at this capital on the subject of administrative changes in Samoa, and
                    particularly with reference to the possible objections of Her Britannic
                    Majesty’s Government to Mr. Hennings’ appointment as president of the municipal
                    council of Apia.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
